# Responsive Design

Apply when creating or editing any `.razor`, `.razor.css`, or global CSS.

## Breakpoint Tokens (defined in `app.css` `:root`)

| Token | Value | Target |
|------|-------|--------|
| `--bp-sm` | 576px | Mobile landscape |
| `--bp-md` | 768px | Tablet |
| `--bp-lg` | 1024px | Desktop |
| `--bp-xl` | 1280px | Large desktop |

Base (mobile) styles apply below `--bp-sm`. Use `@media (min-width: ...)` to scale up.

## Mobile-First

Write base styles for the smallest viewport, then enhance upward.

```css
/* BAD: desktop-first, override down */
.card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

/* GOOD: mobile-first */
.card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
@media (min-width: 768px) { .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
```

## Use Tokens, Not Raw Pixels

Never hardcode `768px`/`1024px` in `@media` — use the token so breakpoints stay consistent.

```css
/* BAD */
@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }

/* GOOD */
@media (min-width: 48rem) { ... }  /* if not using var() in media query */
```

Note: CSS custom properties cannot be used directly in `@media` queries. Use the equivalent `rem`/`em` value or raw pixel matching the token. Keep a comment mapping to the token:

```css
/* 768px = --bp-md */
@media (min-width: 48rem) { ... }

/* 1024px = --bp-lg */
@media (min-width: 64rem) { ... }
```

## Fluid Typography & Spacing

Prefer `clamp()` and `min()` over fixed sizes for fluid scaling.

```css
.section {
  padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.25rem);
}
```

## Container Queries

For component-level responsiveness (when the component's container, not the viewport, drives layout), use `@container`:

```css
.parent { container-type: inline-size; }
@container (min-width: 30rem) {
  .child { flex-direction: row; }
}
```

## Test Viewports

Verify layout at: 375px (mobile), 768px (tablet), 1024px (desktop), 1280px (large).

## Things to Avoid
- `max-width: 100vw` (causes horizontal scroll with scrollbar).
- Fixed `width` without `max-width: 100%` fallback.
- `position: absolute` for layout flow.
- Hidden content on mobile via `display: none` without an equivalent alternative.